{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-18_14-39-49-dragonboat_raft-real-run && python3 -c \\\"\nimport json\ns=json.load(open('state.json'))\nfor v in s['interpretations']:\n    if v['id'].startswith('fc13304'):\n        print(json.dumps(v,indent=1))\n\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"{\n \"id\": \"fc13304ecd544921af7108175e70fcd5-interpretation-0\",\n \"investigation_id\": \"7e17be3eac204967962a1e20e3dfc907-question-0\",\n \"experiment_id\": null,\n \"source_ids\": [\n  \"leader-heartbeat-resp\",\n  \"lw-remote-lookup\",\n  \"broadcast-heartbeat-hint\",\n  \"peer-response-filter\",\n  \"readindex-confirm\",\n  \"membership-add-existing\",\n  \"membership-add-removed\",\n  \"membership-becoming-observer\",\n  \"membership-handle-config-change\",\n  \"raft-remove-node\",\n  \"raft-restore-role-guard\"\n ],\n \"executions\": {\n  \"ec7794827f40455b8a20ef667e3b7461\": [\n   1,\n   2,\n   3\n  ],\n  \"9d3580ca517b4e708e5b3c8c63d670ef\": [\n   2,\n   3\n  ]\n },\n \"conclusion\": \"explained\",\n \"defect_claim\": \"refuted\",\n \"rationale\": \"The suspicion is refuted for the captured legal paths, although the low-level code alone would count it. handleLeaderHeartbeatResp confirms when a heartbeat response carries a nonzero hint, lw admits observer responses, and readIndex.confirm counts the responding node without checking whether it is currently a voter. That is the plausible weakness. The legal transition path does not create the needed state: membership rejects AddObserver or AddWitness for a current address; RemoveNode deletes the node from remotes, observers, and witnesses and marks it removed; isAddRemovedNode rejects re-adding that ID as any role; and raft.restore panics if a non-observer or non-witness local node appears in the snapshot's observer or witness set. In addition, broadcastHeartbeatMessageWithHint sends nonzero-context heartbeats only to votingMembers and sends observer heartbeats only for the zero context. A delayed response from a removed voter is therefore ignored because lw no longer finds it in any role map, and a delayed nonzero context cannot come from an observer under legal transitions. The rejoining-as-observer path is blocked by membership. The admission layers are now measured as well: with one read queued at a leader for voters {1,2,3}, a confirming heartbeat response from node 4, which sits in no role map, left the queue unchanged both when delivered through the Peer and when handed straight to the raft state machine, while the same response from voter 3 confirmed the context and produced a reply for the requester. Under a live removal, voters 1 and 2 first applied a RemoveNode for node 3; a read queued afterwards produced no reply when the confirming response came from removed node 3 and one reply when it came from current voter 2. The conclusion is a protective-mechanism negative result, not a claim that arbitrary direct map mutation or a malicious observer is safe; those are outside the admitted scenario and would still expose the low-level counting behavior.\",\n \"answers\": {},\n \"knowledge\": [\n  {\n   \"entry_id\": \"7e17be3eac204967962a1e20e3dfc907-knowledge-0\",\n   \"revision\": 1,\n   \"assertion\": \"Legal transitions prevent a former voter from retaining a voter-issued nonzero ReadIndex context as an observer.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"entry_id\": \"13e3384fae704dfcb6262b4d270ed548-knowledge-0\",\n   \"revision\": 1,\n   \"assertion\": \"A response from a sender outside every role map left the pending read unconfirmed at both admission layers, while a current voter's response confirmed it.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"entry_id\": \"fc13304ecd544921af7108175e70fcd5-knowledge-0\",\n   \"revision\": 1,\n   \"assertion\": \"After a RemoveNode applied on the remaining voters, the removed node's confirming response produced no reply while a current voter's response confirmed the read.\"\n  }\n ],\n \"counterevidence\": [\n  \"The low-level path does not check voter eligibility in readIndex.confirm; it counts any nonzero-hint response that lw admits.\",\n  \"Observers are admitted by lw for heartbeat responses and are not filtered out by readIndex.confirm.\",\n  \"The refutation depends on the legal membership guards and nonzero-hint routing, not on the absence of these low-level behaviors.\",\n  \"Both admission layers reject an unadmitted sender in the measured execution, so the counting behavior in readIndex.confirm is only reachable for a sender one of those layers admits.\",\n  \"In the live-removal receipt the removed node's response produced no reply while the current voter's response did, so the counting in readIndex.confirm is not reachable from a node the applied transition removed.\"\n ],\n \"limitations\": [\n  \"Direct mutation of the raft role maps, an operator restarting a node with a role inconsistent with cluster membership, forged heartbeat responses, or a custom transport that changes admission are excluded.\",\n  \"The live-removal receipt applies the removal through Peer.ApplyConfigChange on the remaining voters only; node 3 does not run it, and no transport, persistence or restart path is exercised.\",\n  \"The established main finding remains separate: a legal follower-originated ReadIndex batch can receive another request's context and fail to complete.\"\n ],\n \"joint_history\": \"\",\n \"failure_attribution\": null,\n \"operation_id\": \"fc13304ecd544921af7108175e70fcd5\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-18_14-39-49-dragonboat_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nu = {\n \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Correct the ReadIndex membership-filter entry. Re-reading the broadcast path shows votingMembers() is the union of remotes and witnesses, so witnesses are addressed by the hint-carrying heartbeat and their acknowledgements count in the same quorums as voters. The previous statement wrongly said witnesses are not addressed and treated the send-side filter as excluding them. The corrected account keeps the measured and source-supported part: observers receive a heartbeat only with a zero context, so they cannot echo a nonzero hint, and a sender absent from every role map is dropped by the lw admission lookup before readIndex.confirm runs, which is why the removed-voter and unknown-sender responses produced no confirmation.\\\",\n \\\"sources\\\": [\n  {\\\"id\\\": \\\"voting-members-count\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"internal/raft/raft.go\\\", \\\"start_line\\\": 374, \\\"end_line\\\": 381, \\\"kind\\\": \\\"code_observation\\\"},\n  {\\\"id\\\": \\\"voting-members-map\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"internal/raft/raft.go\\\", \\\"start_line\\\": 418, \\\"end_line\\\": 428, \\\"kind\\\": \\\"code_observation\\\"}\n ],\n \\\"knowledge\\\": [\n  {\n   \\\"id\\\": \\\"9652c745a742422d9a1d90eeb6852356-knowledge-0\\\",\n   \\\"kind\\\": \\\"behavior\\\",\n   \\\"statement\\\": \\\"When a ReadIndex request is pending, broadcastHeartbeatMessage uses readIndex.peepCtx as the heartbeat context and broadcastHeartbeatMessageWithHint sends that hint-carrying heartbeat to every member of votingMembers(), which is the union of remotes and witnesses; observers are sent a heartbeat only when the context is zero. numVotingMembers() is len(remotes)+len(witnesses), and both quorum() and the commit path use it, so a witness acknowledgement counts toward the read quorum and the commit quorum alike. On the leader, a HeartbeatResp is admitted through lw, which resolves the sender against the current remotes, observers and witnesses maps and drops the message when it is in none of them; handleLeaderHeartbeatResp then passes a nonzero hint to handleReadIndexLeaderConfirmation, and readIndex.confirm performs no further role check.\\\",\n   \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"The node is leader with at least one pending ReadIndex request, the role maps reflect the current configuration, and a heartbeat response arrives from a node that is currently a voter, an observer, a witness, or in no role map.\\\",\n   \\\"source_ids\\\": [\n    \\\"heartbeat-hint-voters-only\\\",\n    \\\"leader-heartbeat-resp-admission\\\",\n    \\\"readindex-confirm-count\\\",\n    \\\"voting-members-count\\\",\n    \\\"voting-members-map\\\"\n   ],\n   \\\"changed_premise\\\": \\\"The earlier statement said witnesses are not addressed by the hint-carrying heartbeat and that the send-side filter excluded them from the acknowledgement count. votingMembers() includes witnesses, so they receive the hint and their acknowledgements count in both the read and commit quorums; the only sender kept from echoing a nonzero hint is an observer, which receives a heartbeat only with a zero context, and a sender outside every role map is dropped by the admission lookup.\\\",\n   \\\"affected_uses\\\": []\n  }\n ]\n}\nopen('update.json','w').write(json.dumps(u, indent=2) + \\\"\\\\n\\\")\nPY\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance && .venv/bin/consensus-assurance validate --run runs/2026-10-18_14-39-49-dragonboat_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -5\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
